  "idea": "How to split your computer screen into two clean windows for multitasking",
  "text": "Stop minimizing and maximizing windows fifty times an hour while working on your computer. Constantly clicking between background tabs to cross-reference data scrambles your thoughts and causes silly copy errors. Losing visual context between overlapping applications wastes minutes every time you need to confirm numbers. Press Windows Key plus the Left or Right Arrow to snap windows cleanly side by side. This gives you instant dual-window multitasking without extra hardware.",
